            "**Result.** A typical team member attends the daily meeting, the service delivery review and the retrospective: 5.0 + 1.5 + 1.0 = **7.5 hours a month, or 5.0% of 150 working hours**. The team member who also attends replenishment spends 9.5 hours (6.3%). The team lead, who attends every cadence, spends about 11.9 hours (7.9%).",
            "**What the team does with this.** The calculation makes the cost of coordination visible and gives the team a basis for pruning. It also shows where the effort goes: two-thirds of a typical member's meeting time is the daily meeting, so keeping that meeting to 15 minutes matters more than trimming the monthly reviews. The figures assume full attendance and no overruns; a daily meeting that habitually runs to 25 minutes adds over three hours per person per month.",
